Two P2 findings raised during review are now addressed:

- Pre-candidate resume could adopt unexpected rows. Resume now requires exact original row multisets and table inventory before candidate creation; afterward, the atomically recorded digest covers added rows. The interruption regression exercises the original gap.
- Bundled unique indexes could reject valid captured rows before reconciliation. Mismatching nonconstraint defaults are now removed before loading rows. Captured definitions are installed afterward and compared exactly, within the transaction. New regressions distinguish the changed uniqueness semantics.

The reviewed code captures all installed catalog index names and definitions, binds them to the checkpoint, preserves quoted names and predicate literals when rebinding the indexed relation, and verifies the exact inventory on restore and resume. The importer round-trip regression checks rejection of duplicate DOI and arXiv values. Neo4j added-object rejection and recorded isolated replay quarantine disposition are consistent with the stated continuation.

